  "slug": "city-qkd-3d90",
  "summary": "New preprints report a four-city entanglement QKD network, CV entanglement over deployed fibre and comb-based shared infrastructure, alongside finite-key proofs.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the transition of quantum communication from laboratory testbeds to field-deployed links with rigorous finite-size security accounting. A four-city Slovak entanglement-based QKD network delivers keys in real time and is benchmarked against finite-key bounds. Continuous-variable entanglement is distributed over deployed metropolitan fibre (23 km and 450 m) using independent coherent receivers and digital processing. An optical-frequency-comb infrastructure unifies precision timing and 100 Mbit/s classical data on a shared 100 km fibre. On the theory side, variable-length MDI QKD gains a finite-size proof that accounts for source imperfections, with key rates over horizontal links beyond 80 km. Finite-key MIMO CV-QKD is analysed for satellite channels. Related work extends protocols and media: frequency-bin quantum secret sharing with 20 MHz basis switching, and pre-amplified two-mode squeezed microwave states over open air. Adjacent photonics results address postselection-free CHSH violation and fusion-based computing under partial photon distinguishability.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-23"
}
